Two new optional auxillary headers have been added to comp.sources.games
postings.  The first one "Patch-To:" lists a volume and issue number that
a posted patch applies to.  This can provide extra help for automatic
archivers to ensure that the patch gets archived with the original
source (for archive sites that save files by vol/issue).  The format of
the "Patch-To:" line is:

	Patch-To: Volume v, Issue i
or
	Patch-To: Volume v, Issue i-j

The second optional header is "Superseeds:".  This is used when posting
an updated version of a program that was previously posted.  The format
of the "Superseeds:" line is:

	Superseeds: archive-name; Volume n, Issue i
or
	Superseeds: archive-name; Volume n, Issue i-j

The Superseeds entry is helpful for cleaning archives by providing a
pointer to previous versions that (may) be deleted from the archive.
As always, feedback and suggestions for improvement are welcome.

